仅仅一年后，也就是1969年，她就为自己的专辑《灵魂姐妹》录制了翻唱版本。

878
00:37:48.420 --> 00:37:50.020
I had to hear it.
我必须得听听看。

879
00:37:50.340 --> 00:37:51.560
Sam, will you play it?
萨姆，你能放一下吗？

880
00:38:22.980 --> 00:38:24.280
It's so good, isn't it?
太好听了，不是吗？

881
00:38:24.400 --> 00:38:24.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

882
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:26.360
She always gives me chills.
她总是让我起鸡皮疙瘩。

883
00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:30.200
Dolly Parton also did a cover in 1996 for her album Treasures.
多莉·帕顿也在1996年为她的专辑《珍宝》翻唱过。

884
00:38:30.340 --> 00:38:32.000
And it is also a gem.
那也是一首瑰宝。

885
00:38:32.180 --> 00:38:33.100
Do you want to hear that one?
你想听听那个版本吗？

886
00:38:33.280 --> 00:38:33.720
Yes!
想！

887
00:38:48.980 --> 00:39:03.140
I can listen to these women sing anything.
我可以听这些女性唱任何歌。

888
00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:04.260
They're legends.
她们是传奇。

889
00:39:04.520 --> 00:39:06.780
Legends in our podcast today.
今天我们播客里的传奇。

890
00:39:07.020 --> 00:39:08.860
Do we need to hear Dusty's?
我们需要听听达斯蒂的版本吗？

891
00:39:09.460 --> 00:39:11.100
I think we need to hear Dusty's.
我觉得我们需要听听达斯蒂的版本。

892
00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:12.760
I mean, we have to hear Dusty's.
我是说，我们必须得听听达斯蒂的版本。

893
00:39:12.980 --> 00:39:14.880
It's Son of a Preacher Man Day today.
今天简直是《牧师之子》主题日。

894
00:39:15.080 --> 00:39:16.940
I mean, I just want to hear all of them.
我是说，我真想把所有的版本都听一遍。

895
00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:24.480
I feel so embarrassed that I even attempted to sing it at all to recreate the scene with Ryan.
我为自己竟然试图唱这首歌来重现和瑞安的那一幕感到尴尬。

896
00:39:24.780 --> 00:39:25.900
I am so sorry.
我真的很抱歉。

897
00:39:30.900 --> 00:39:31.300
Ha!
哈！

898
00:39:43.340 --> 00:39:50.480
Lord knows to my surprise, the only one who could ever reach me was the Son of a Preacher Man.
上帝知道，令我惊讶的是，唯一能触动我的人竟然是那位牧师之子。

899
00:39:50.800 --> 00:39:51.820
The only boy.
唯一的男孩。

900
00:39:51.960 --> 00:39:52.480
All right.
好了。

901
00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:53.440
Oh, so good.
噢，太棒了。

902
00:39:53.600 --> 00:39:53.880
All right.
好吧。

903
00:39:53.960 --> 00:39:54.260
All right.
好吧。

904
00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:55.820
Here's what I have to say.
我有话要说。

905
00:39:56.200 --> 00:40:02.420
Kudos to John Hurley and Ronnie Wilkins, because when you write a song that can be sung by all of
向约翰·赫尔利和罗尼·威尔金斯致敬，因为当你写出一首歌，能被所有

906
00:40:02.420 --> 00:40:06.180
these different people with their different spins on it and their different arrangements.
这些不同的人用他们不同的风格和编曲来演唱时，

907
00:40:06.180 --> 00:40:09.160
And it still knocks your socks off every time.
而且每次听都依然让人惊艳不已，

908
00:40:09.300 --> 00:40:10.480
You have written a good song.
那你就是写出了一首好歌。

909
00:40:10.620 --> 00:40:10.780
Yep.
没错。

910
00:40:11.200 --> 00:40:16.620
One last thing I want to say about Son of a Preacher Man is that when Melora sang it,
关于《牧师之子》我最后想说的是，当梅洛拉演唱这首歌时，

911
00:40:16.900 --> 00:40:18.840
she improvised the snapping.
她即兴加入了打响指的动作。

912
00:40:19.300 --> 00:40:20.500
And you know what?
你猜怎么着？

913
00:40:20.700 --> 00:40:23.360
It about got me on the floor.
我差点笑趴在地上。

914
00:40:23.540 --> 00:40:29.920
We were so trying to suppress laughter that one more thing was like the tipping point,
我们当时拼命忍住不笑，而那个动作简直就是压死骆驼的最后一根稻草，

915
00:40:30.120 --> 00:40:30.400
you know?
你懂吗？

916
00:40:30.540 --> 00:40:30.800
Yes.
是的。

917
00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:35.340
And so as she's swaying and singing, when she just starts doing that snap, I was like,
所以当她摇摆着身体唱歌，突然开始打响指时，我心想，

918
00:40:35.420 --> 00:40:36.660
oh, Lord, I'm not going to make it.
天哪，我快撑不住了。

919
00:40:36.800 --> 00:40:37.760
I am not going to make it.
我真的快撑不住了。

920
00:40:38.080 --> 00:40:42.760
There are really great scripted talking heads of people reacting to it.
剧本里确实有一些很棒的采访片段，记录了人们对此的反应。

921
00:40:42.880 --> 00:40:46.620
And Stan Lee had a great one where he was like, I used to like that song.
斯坦·李就有一个很棒的片段，他说，我以前挺喜欢那首歌的。

922
00:40:50.380 --> 00:40:53.200
Well, Jim is going to try to describe it to Pam.
嗯，吉姆打算向帕姆描述那首歌。

923
00:40:53.820 --> 00:40:57.340
She's at the laundromat and she can't hear anything he's saying.
当时她在洗衣店，根本听不清他在说什么。

924
00:40:57.580 --> 00:40:59.940
Why couldn't she just walk away from the machines, Jenna?
